From 58d922a1072e91c66ef7b1823e3f93f6ec92c806 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:42:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: fit the first GP on the whole log's neighbours with
 evaluations made before the run

With precomputed_evaluations, the first GP was fitted on the start and
the initial design alone, and the loop's first rebuild brought the
evaluations given into its training set under those hyperparameters
until the first refit, which waits until the run has made more than D
evaluations. In a rerun given the log of an earlier run with the same
seed and start, the log holds every point of the initial design, which
is not evaluated again, so the first GP held the start alone, with MATLAB
BADS's definition values, beside hundreds of evaluations near it.

The PI's ruling of 2026-09-29: with evaluations made before the run, the
first GP's hyperparameters are fitted on the incumbent's neighbours in
the whole log, chosen and capped as a rebuild chooses them.
_init_optimization_ keeps the initial step (the fit on the start and the
design, or the definition values on one distinct point) and then,
within the gp_init stage (as gp_init/gp_rebuild), rebuilds the GP with
local_gp_fitting and a refit, once. That is the loop's rebuild: it
re-centres the priors on the training set (the mean's at its 90th
percentile), starts the refit from the hyperparameters just set, sets
the refit's geometry, and on a failure hands on the GP of the start and
the design, marked for a rebuild with a refit at the first poll. The
refit is not recorded in lastfitgp, so that the loop's refits keep their
rule (func_count > D), and the schedule of the fits leaves the
evaluations given out of n_eff as before. Choosing the initial rows as
the rebuild would and fitting once was not taken: it would need the
choice of the neighbours outside local_gp_fitting, would fit under the
definition's priors rather than the rebuild's re-centred ones, and would
leave out the rebuild's handling of a failure.

Without evaluations made before the run nothing moves: the rebuild, and
its draws from bads.rng, happen only when the log holds them
(fingerprint.py 4146a986863602cb with one BLAS thread and with the
default; replay.py check against f6c13872, 8 of 8 runs identical;
make_oracle_fixtures.py --check --exact, and --against a --dump of
f6c13872, pass).

Tests (test_bads_precomputed_evaluations.py): two tests asserted that
the first GP holds the start and the design alone, and are replaced:
test_the_gp_holds_the_evaluations_made_before by
test_the_first_gp_holds_the_evaluations_made_before (the 12 evaluations
given and the run's 5, with the refit's geometry), and
test_the_first_fit_leaves_out_many_evaluations by
test_the_first_gp_takes_the_nearest_of_many_evaluations (of 1000, the
nearest, capped as a rebuild caps them).
test_the_training_schedule_leaves_them_out sees two fits, both with
gp_train_n_init starts. New: test_a_rerun_starts_on_a_fitted_gp and
test_a_failed_first_rebuild_leaves_the_gp_of_the_design; and, in
test_stage_times.py, test_stages_with_evaluations_made_before at the
three uncertainty levels (the _make_bads of test_gp_update_failures.py
takes precomputed_evaluations).

Records: KD-B1-15 and KD-B6-5, AGENTS.md's FunctionLogger bullet,
init_and_train_gp's docstring, and the changelog's entries for
precomputed_evaluations and for targets without spread.

